what this file says:
 1. oneRecordEach_iff_keepingDraws. "Each distinction has one record, and a protocol draws it exactly when
    it maintains that record" holds if and only if "a protocol that maintains every record a family needs
    draws the family" (KeepingDraws, clause (K) of pass 115). So the ruling of 05:29 HST, with the other
    direction of the primitive, is clause (K): no more and no less.
 2. drawingCarries_of_oneRecordEach. With one record each, a distinction drawn by a protocol is drawn by
    every protocol that maintains at least the same records. That is B06's sentence 6 as far as drawing
    goes.
 3. record_subset_needs, needs_singleton_eq_record. A family needs the record of each of its members; and
    where some protocol maintains exactly the record of a distinction, that record is what the distinction
    needs when held alone.
 4. exists_fewest_records, familyCost_eq_bill_of_fewest. At epsilon the cost of a family is attained: it is
    the bill of a protocol that draws the family and keeps the fewest records.
 5. marginal_step_ge_eps_of_bill, marginalFloor_of_bill. At epsilon, with epsilon positive, adding a
    support-novel distinction raises the cost of a family by at least epsilon: B05's declared form
    (APFB05.MarginalFloor), with the same epsilon. Only clause (E) is used. Clauses (K) and (R), the
    ruling, B03 and the occupant statement are not used.
 6. familyCost_eq_eps_mul_card_of_exact_keeper. With (K) and (E), where a protocol maintains exactly the
    records a family needs, the cost of the family is epsilon times the number of records it needs.
what this file does NOT say:
 - That clause (E) holds. It is the bill as a sum at one price for every protocol. The bill as a sum is an
   adopted reading of 2026-11-14 that the author kept out of the inputs on 2026-11-17 04:25 HST, and
   "each record it keeps costs epsilon" is said in B06 of the occupant only. The Supplement's case study
   bills trials as well as records (v9.28:1969-1975, 6043).
 - That B05 is no longer needed as an input. That is the author's to rule, and it turns on clause (E).
 - Anything about words, steps or states. B06's sentence 12 is not reached here.
 - That sufficiency carries for sets of records that no protocol uses (the typing of sentence 6 on file,
   SufficiencyCarries). See Thm_APFB06_one_record_each_in_the_worlds for a small case where it fails.
 - No lane. No claim that the transfer is forced, that the carrier gap is closed or narrowed, or that
   Born is derived.
axioms: within propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. No sorry.
